1 " Forms designate and differentiate the things, form is the principle of existential multiplicity. When the things descend from the One-or when the Form-giver gives form to the creatures-they appear as diverse and many because of the multiplicity of their forms

2. " In contrast, matter per se is a single, simple, undifferentiated, imperceptible reality. It has no form, so it has no quality, attribute, description, or designation, except for a certain impalpable presence in conjunction with form. "

Matter has nothing of its own, and whatever appears to our senses comes from the forms that have descended from the One. Indeed, for Plotinus, matter is an invisible mirror that displays the forms and can never be seen itself, because it is absolute nonexistence. "

Thus matter allows the individual forms that are unified in the First Intellect to be differentiated, deployed, and perceived in the cosmos

anyone speaks of worlds in the PLURAL, we think the plurality is horizontal and quantitative. 
Even the speculation about a diversity of worlds and dimensions that goes on in modern physics pictures "physical" worlds since there can be no other domain studied by "physics."
Muslim thinkers typically understand worlds in terms of a vertical hierarchy that quickly transcends any sort of physicality. This does not mean that Muslims have not imagined a plurality of horizontal worlds, but this is a SECONDARY idea. "

from the Necessary in Existence and the nearest to nonexistence.”
